# Host canonicalization (4.19.2): the apex was serving the full site as a
# second origin — duplicate pages in Search Console and an independent
# service worker/cache that could wedge separately from www (the 2026-08-17
# stuck-shell incident was on the apex). Full-URL sources are the
# Pages-native way to redirect across hosts. Since 11.0.3 this line is THE
# apex redirect: the apex is no longer a Worker route, because a Worker over
# its daily quota answered 429 for the apex robots.txt and Google stopped
# crawling the whole domain. Must stay FIRST: rules match top-down.
https://sirimillavinay.online/* https://www.sirimillavinay.online/:splat 301

# Hashed build assets must NEVER fall back to the SPA shell: an HTML body
# cached under the /assets/* one-year header bricks that chunk URL. That is
# NOT done here (8.5.2): Pages accepts only 200 and 301-308 in this file, so
# the old `/assets/*  /assets-404.txt  404` line was silently dropped and a
# missing chunk kept answering 200 + the SPA shell + max-age=31536000. A 200
# rewrite is no fix either — it overrides the real chunks too. The guard is
# public/assets/404.html: Pages answers a miss under /assets/ with the nearest
# 404.html (404, no-store) while app routes keep the SPA fallback, because
# there is no top-level 404.html.

# Route aliases — legacy/guessable paths land on the real pages.
/downloads  /offline  301
/listen-together  /together  301
# 8.4.0: the standalone Ads page is gone (placements now sit at the end of
# song, artist, album and hub pages); old links land on Discover.
/ads  /discover  301

# Status page — status.sirimillavinay.online lands on the standalone status
# app (public/status/, plain static files — fully independent of the SPA
# shell, so listeners can check on VinaX even when the app misbehaves).
# Pages only honors host-based sources for REDIRECTS, not 200 rewrites, so
# the subdomain 301s onto the real /status/ path, which static files serve.
https://status.sirimillavinay.online/ https://status.sirimillavinay.online/status/ 301

/*    /index.html   200
